{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"toolcall_delta","contentIndex":1,"delta":"{\"i\":\"Writing repair report\",\"path\":\"<SOURCE_EVIDENCE_ROOT>/trials/099-083-monorepo-interface-repair-omp-a02-r01/hb-work/omp/gpt-5.4/oc-bench-v2-083-monorepo-interface-repair-gpt-5.4-20260831-133423-eacf6630/workspace/out/interface_fix_report.md\",\"content\":\"# Interface Fix Report\\n\\n## Root cause\\n`catalog` migrated product pricing from a legacy `price_cents` field to `Product.price: Money(amount_cents, currency)`, but `orders.adapter` still read `product.price_cents` / `product[\\\"price_cents\\\"]` and only guessed currency from top-level fields. That broke downstream order pricing for `catalog.Product` objects and left currency handling split across incompatible shapes.\\n\\n## Changed files\\n- `packages/orders/orders/adapter.py`\\n  - Added `_price_data(product)` as the boundary adapter for both supported product shapes.\\n  - Reads new `Money` pricing from object or dictionary `price` values.\\n  - Preserves legacy dictionary support for `price_cents` plus top-level `currency`.\\n- `packages/orders/orders/service.py`\\n  - Kept mixed-currency validation in the order layer.\\n  - Improved the raised error to name both conflicting currencies.\\n\\n## Verification command\\nExecuted from `/workspace/in/shopmono` with a temporary local shim for missing host tools:\\n\\n`python -m pytest tests`\\n\\nResult: `5 passed`\\n\\nAdditional smoke check: legacy product dictionaries still return `300 USD` through `orders.adapter.price_cents()` / `orders.adapter.currency()`.\\n\"}"}}
{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"toolcall_end","contentIndex":1,"toolCall":{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_BVDyf0zPWy6SCcMXkexMroei|fc_07e673ba582ffc0b016a95bba2552887d29ea0921617e4cb90","name":"write","arguments":{"i":"Writing repair report","path":"<SOURCE_EVIDENCE_ROOT>/trials/099-083-monorepo-interface-repair-omp-a02-r01/hb-work/omp/gpt-5.4/oc-bench-v2-083-monorepo-interface-repair-gpt-5.4-20260831-133423-eacf6630/workspace/out/interface_fix_report.md","content":"# Interface Fix Report\n\n## Root cause\n`catalog` migrated product pricing from a legacy `price_cents` field to `Product.price: Money(amount_cents, currency)`, but `orders.adapter` still read `product.price_cents` / `product[\"price_cents\"]` and only guessed currency from top-level fields. That broke downstream order pricing for `catalog.Product` objects and left currency handling split across incompatible shapes.\n\n## Changed files\n- `packages/orders/orders/adapter.py`\n  - Added `_price_data(product)` as the boundary adapter for both supported product shapes.\n  - Reads new `Money` pricing from object or dictionary `price` values.\n  - Preserves legacy dictionary support for `price_cents` plus top-level `currency`.\n- `packages/orders/orders/service.py`\n  - Kept mixed-currency validation in the order layer.\n  - Improved the raised error to name both conflicting currencies.\n\n## Verification command\nExecuted from `/workspace/in/shopmono` with a temporary local shim for missing host tools:\n\n`python -m pytest tests`\n\nResult: `5 passed`\n\nAdditional smoke check: legacy product dictionaries still return `300 USD` through `orders.adapter.price_cents()` / `orders.adapter.currency()`.\n"}}}}
