{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"text_end","contentIndex":1,"content":"Fixed.\n\nChanges:\n- `packages/orders/orders/adapter.py`\n  - Added `_price_data(product)` as the boundary adapter.\n  - Supports:\n    - new `Product.price: Money`\n    - dict products with `price` as object/dict\n    - legacy dict products with `price_cents`\n  - `price_cents()` and `currency()` now both read from the same normalized source.\n- `packages/orders/orders/service.py`\n  - Preserved mixed-currency rejection.\n  - Error is now explicit: `mixed currencies are not supported: USD and EUR`.\n\nRoot cause:\n- `catalog` moved pricing to `price: Money(amount_cents, currency)`.\n- `orders.adapter` still assumed `price_cents` / top-level `currency`.\n- `reports` depended on `orders.service.price_order()`, so fixing the `orders` boundary restored both packages.\n\nVerification:\n- Smoke check:\n  - `price_order([{\"sku\":\"PEN\",\"quantity\":2},{\"sku\":\"PAD\",\"quantity\":1}], sample_catalog())`\n    → `{'total_cents': 550, 'currency': 'USD'}`\n  - `summarize_orders(...)`\n    → `{'order_count': 2, 'revenue_by_currency': {'USD': 250, 'EUR': 700}}`\n  - mixed-currency order raised:\n    - `ValueError mixed currencies are not supported: USD and EUR`\n  - legacy dict check:\n    - `price_cents(...)`, `currency(...)` → `300 USD`\n- Test command executed from `/workspace/in/shopmono`:\n  - `python -m pytest tests`\n  - Result: `5 passed`\n\nReport:\n- Wrote `interface_fix_report.md` to `/workspace/out/interface_fix_report.md`.\n\nNote:\n- The absolute `/Users/.../workspace/out/...` path was not writable/available in this environment; the mounted workspace output location is `/workspace/out/interface_fix_report.md`."}}
